<title>USA: EPA fines Sherwin-Williams and LTV.</title>
<headline>EPA fines Sherwin-Williams and LTV.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sherwin-Williams Co and LTV Steel Co have agreed to consent decrees calling for millions of dollars in civil penalties and clean-up costs, the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Sherwin-Williams, a paint manufacturer, agreed to pay $4.7 million in civil penalties and $1.1 million towards clean-up areas around a plant in Chicago.</p>
<p>LTV, which operates a coke facility also on the city's south side, will pay $1.25 million in civil penalties and agreed to spend $1.8 million on a project to reduce emissions, EPA officials told a news conference here.</p>
</text>
